          These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of the <strong>TopoQuizz</strong>
          mobile application (the "App") operated by <strong>SHEMED YISRAEL SOFTWARE CREATION LLC</strong>
          ("we," "us," or "our"). By downloading, installing, or using the App, you agree to be bound by
          these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the App.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
        <p>
          TopoQuizz is a mobile learning application for Spanish-speaking medical students, covering topics
          such as anatomy, pharmacology, and related subjects. It is operated by
          <strong>SHEMED YISRAEL SOFTWARE CREATION LLC</strong>.
          Contact: <a href="mailto:administracion@shemayisraelsrl.com">administracion@shemayisraelsrl.com</a>
        </p>

        <h2>2. Eligibility</h2>
        <p>
          You must be at least 18 years old to use the App. By using the App, you represent and warrant
          that you meet this requirement. If you are under 18, you may not use the App.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Account Registration</h2>
        <p>
          To access certain features, you must create an account. You may register directly or use a
          third-party login provider such as <strong>Google</strong> or <strong>Facebook</strong>. You agree to:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide accurate and complete information during registration</li>
          <li>Keep your credentials secure and confidential</li>
          <li>Notify us immediately of any unauthorized use of your account</li>
          <li>Be responsible for all activity that occurs under your account</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We reserve the right to suspend or terminate accounts that violate these Terms or that we
          reasonably believe pose a risk to other users or to our systems.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Use of the App</h2>
        <p>You agree to use the App only for lawful purposes and in accordance with these Terms. You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the App in any way that violates applicable laws or regulations</li>
